    {
      "id": "3kymk61",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Rise of the Gupta Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The chapter covers the origin, rise, and consolidation of the Gupta Empire.",
        "Samudragupta ruled from 335 to 375 CE, expanding the territorial reach of the empire.",
        "Chandragupta II (Vikramaditya) ruled from 380 to 415 CE, marking a peak in cultural and political influence.",
        "Key topics include Gupta administration, economy, art, architecture, literature, education, science, and technology.",
        "The chapter outlines the factors leading to the decline of the empire alongside high-yield SSC exam facts."
      ],
      "id": "64yz92r"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0a00kff",
      "content": "• The Gupta Empire was founded by Sri Gupta around 240 CE."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fzpqtkh",
      "content": "• The Guptas initially ruled a small kingdom in eastern Uttar Pradesh and Bihar."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ti4ugj",
      "content": "• The real expansion of the empire started with Chandragupta I."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mb7ngfr",
      "content": "• Chandragupta I assumed the title 'Maharajadhiraja'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "exqeewq",
      "content": "• His marriage with Lichchhavi princess Kumaradevi strengthened the Gupta power."
    },
    {
      "id": "iodcwtf",
      "type": "heading",
