    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l2vybby",
      "content": "<img></img>• Agriculture was the main occupation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6ehkk6n",
      "content": "• Land revenue was the main source of income."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "75jdijo",
      "content": "• Trade and commerce flourished during this period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v0874cf",
      "content": "• Gold coins known as 'Dinaras' were issued by Gupta rulers."
    },
    {
      "id": "loalvbd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Art and Architecture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5btm9qr",
      "content": "• Gupta art is considered the classical phase of Indian art."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t4qmgky",
      "content": "• Ajanta caves contain beautiful paintings of the Gupta period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mil9bku",
      "content": "• Temple architecture developed significantly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zpc44lc",
      "content": "• Example: Dashavatara Temple at Deogarh."
    },
    {
      "id": "a8hwuyh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Literature and Education"
    },
